// A SUFFIXED literal is range-checked against its own suffix. It was not: `createIntegerLiteralNode`
// narrowed with a C cast and never compared, so `300i8` became 44 — silently, through `kama check` and
// `kama build` both, with the program exiting 44 and nothing anywhere saying why.
//
// This is the wrong way round from the unsuffixed literal, which always checked: here the author has
// STATED the width, which is more information, not less.
fn int32 main() {
    int8 a = 300i8;   // 300 is not an int8; it was becoming 44
    return cast<int32>(a);
}
